Harmattan build: QtContacts and QtVersit only

QtOrganizer, QtVersitOrganizer and their plugins and QML import are left out: the phone's
calendar is not in Tracker in a shape any organizer backend reads, so they would ship
without one. QtVersit stays, because the QtContacts QML import links it.

The memory plugin gets a PLUGIN_CLASS_NAME, as upstream did after this commit (4b2bdce3, which
names it QMemoryContactsPlugin; this is the real class): without one qmake writes
Qt5Contacts_.cmake, an unnamed plugin target that breaks find_package(Qt5Contacts) in every
CMake app ("_populate_Contacts_plugin_properties Macro invoked with incorrect arguments").

--- a/src/imports/imports.pro
+++ b/src/imports/imports.pro
@@ -1,2 +1,2 @@
 TEMPLATE = subdirs
-SUBDIRS += contacts organizer
+SUBDIRS += contacts
--- a/src/plugins/contacts/memory/memory.pro
+++ b/src/plugins/contacts/memory/memory.pro
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@ TARGET = qtcontacts_memory
 QT = core contacts
 
 PLUGIN_TYPE = contacts
+PLUGIN_CLASS_NAME = QContactMemoryEngineFactory
 load(qt_plugin)
 
 HEADERS += \
--- a/src/plugins/plugins.pro
+++ b/src/plugins/plugins.pro
@@ -1,2 +1,2 @@
 TEMPLATE = subdirs
-SUBDIRS += contacts organizer versit
+SUBDIRS += contacts
--- a/src/src.pro
+++ b/src/src.pro
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
 TEMPLATE = subdirs
 CONFIG  += ordered
-SUBDIRS = contacts organizer versit versitorganizer plugins
+SUBDIRS = contacts versit plugins
 qtHaveModule(qml): SUBDIRS += imports
